Problem Statement
1.	Create a base class Member with:
o	Data members:
name, age, phoneNumber, address, salary
o	Method:
printSalary() → prints the member’s salary.
2.	Create two subclasses:
o	Employee → adds specialization
o	Manager → adds department
3.	Create objects of both Employee and Manager, assign values, and print all details including salary.
Requirements
•	Demonstrate inheritance in Java.
•	Access and print both base class and derived class members.
•	Implement method overriding or extension where appropriate.
•	Use encapsulation principles (private variables and public setters/getters are optional for simplicity).
